id: pm-jkjt
title: Reject ambiguous event durations with explicit minute and month units
description: "Dogfood GH-450: relative-parser maps m=months (PR#263) so a 5-minute standup becomes a 5-month meeting with no warning; minutes exist as 'min' (pm-zoe4). Needs an ambiguity guard or convention flip. Duplicate check: pm-zoe4 (closed) added min granularity only; pm-o3fh moves the shortcuts but not the parser; no open overlap."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: agent-ux,bug,calendar,gh-issue
created_at: "2026-07-06T08:03:09.588Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-22T05:06:28.516Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-18T03:55:52.493Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-18T03:55:52.493Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "Bare 'm' duration can no longer silently mean months (error-with-hint or convention flip with deprecation window, decision recorded under pm-m2u1); duration units exhaustively documented; parser spec covers m/min/mo"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Shared SDK event validation rejects ambiguous bare m durations before any mutation and accepts explicit min and mo units; create, update and package shortcuts share the contract and guidance."
expected_result: Five minutes requires 5min and five months requires 5mo; ambiguous input cannot silently create months or partially mutate items.
actual_result: "Red-first rejection tests pass across scheduling, create and update; temporary Node/Bun sessions verified unchanged item metadata on refusal, explicit end precedence and month-end clamping."
